  "articleBody": "Thinking about adding a guest home? It’s a fantastic way to add flexibility and value to your property, whether it's for visitors, aging family members, or even a potential rental income. But before you dive in, let's chat about what makes a property truly ready for a secondary dwelling. Zen Tiny Homes specializes in custom designs that fit your specific needs, focusing on livability and intelligent use of space, not just shrinking a standard home.\n\nFirst off, consider your property's size and zoning. While tiny homes offer efficient footprints, local regulations in San Diego County (City and unincorporated areas) can vary quite a bit regarding setbacks and coverage. Understanding these rules early on is crucial to avoid headaches down the line. Next, think about access and utilities. Will your guest home need separate utilities, or can it tap into existing ones? We always start with a property assessment to figure out these details from the get-go. Then, what's the purpose? If it's a rental, you'll want features that appeal to a broad audience, like a full kitchen and private entrance. If it's for family, customization can be much more personal. Finally, consider how the guest home integrates with your existing property aesthetically and functionally. You want it to enhance, not detract from, your main residence.\n\nReady to explore the possibilities for your backyard? Let's talk about how a custom-designed Zen Tiny Home can transform your property into something truly special.",
